WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.215 --> 00:00:02.801
- When I was seven years old,
I murdered the tooth fairy,

00:00:02.801 --> 00:00:05.317
and this is that story.

00:00:05.317 --> 00:00:08.474
The year was 2001 and I had
just lost my first tooth.

00:00:08.474 --> 00:00:10.549
I was one of the first people
in my class to lose a tooth

00:00:10.549 --> 00:00:13.092
so it was a really big deal.

00:00:13.092 --> 00:00:15.775
Everyone was very impressed
as I held my tooth up

00:00:15.775 --> 00:00:17.540
proudly for them to see.

00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:20.280
I imagine that's probably
what Beyonce feels like

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:23.121
when she points her
microphone to the crowd.

00:00:23.121 --> 00:00:24.477
When I got home from school that day,

00:00:24.477 --> 00:00:27.084
I showed my mom and my siblings my tooth.

00:00:27.084 --> 00:00:31.979
That is when my mom sat me
down and told me all about

00:00:31.979 --> 00:00:34.062
this elusive tooth fairy.

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:38.546
Tonight I was going to put
my tooth under my pillow,

00:00:38.546 --> 00:00:41.633
go to sleep and then a
tiny fairy was going to

00:00:41.633 --> 00:00:45.196
sneak into my house, take the tooth,

00:00:45.196 --> 00:00:46.972
and then leave me money in its place.

00:00:46.972 --> 00:00:48.690
I had a lot of questions.

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:51.267
What happens if I'm not
asleep when she comes?

00:00:51.267 --> 00:00:52.983
What if I have to talk to her?

00:00:52.983 --> 00:00:54.458
Does she speak English?

00:00:54.458 --> 00:00:55.699
What language does she speak?

00:00:55.699 --> 00:00:57.677
She lives in Antarctica, right?

00:00:57.677 --> 00:00:59.091
How many visits does she make a night?

00:00:59.091 --> 00:01:00.483
What if she can't find my tooth?

00:01:00.483 --> 00:01:02.698
What if my head is just too
heavy for her tiny little body

00:01:02.698 --> 00:01:03.613
to lift up?

00:01:03.613 --> 00:01:06.072
What if she just forgets to come?

00:01:06.072 --> 00:01:07.557
Okay, listen.

00:01:07.557 --> 00:01:10.000
I was already terrified of Santa,

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:13.217
a man who left me multiple gifts a year.

00:01:13.217 --> 00:01:15.938
Don't even get me started
on the man-sized rabbit

00:01:15.938 --> 00:01:17.958
who leaves me chocolate every Easter.

00:01:17.958 --> 00:01:21.708
Not a mythical creature, but
I was also pretty terrified

00:01:21.708 --> 00:01:22.701
of my mail man.

00:01:22.701 --> 00:01:26.133
As you can tell, I was
a very anxious child.

00:01:26.133 --> 00:01:27.671
And an equally anxious adult.

00:01:27.671 --> 00:01:30.173
I hated talking to people I didn't know.

00:01:30.173 --> 00:01:32.614
I hated talking to people
I did know for that matter.

00:01:32.614 --> 00:01:35.558
I was so shy that my mom
resorted to paying me

00:01:35.558 --> 00:01:38.594
25 cents every time I
said hi back to anyone

00:01:38.594 --> 00:01:39.697
who greeted me.

00:01:39.697 --> 00:01:43.864
Instead of meeting them with
this weird, awkward silence.

00:01:45.881 --> 00:01:46.919
Back to the tooth.

00:01:46.919 --> 00:01:49.531
When bedtime finally came,
I knew there was no way

00:01:49.531 --> 00:01:52.556
I was falling asleep anytime soon.

00:01:52.556 --> 00:01:55.079
Since apparently I was
having company that night,

00:01:55.079 --> 00:01:57.806
I put on my favorite pajamas
and I brushed my hair

00:01:57.806 --> 00:01:59.221
before I went to bed.

00:01:59.221 --> 00:02:01.619
I wanted the tooth fairy to think I was

00:02:01.619 --> 00:02:03.388
well dressed and pretty.

00:02:03.388 --> 00:02:06.035
Even at seven years old,
I was a huge narcissist.

00:02:06.035 --> 00:02:08.603
So it's the middle of the
night and I've spent hours

00:02:08.603 --> 00:02:10.006
tossing and turning.

00:02:10.006 --> 00:02:12.883
Honestly I wanted nothing
more than to just pass out

00:02:12.883 --> 00:02:14.709
so I'd miss her completely.

00:02:14.709 --> 00:02:17.059
Luckily at some point, I did fall asleep.

00:02:17.059 --> 00:02:21.059
Cut to the next morning
and something feels off.

00:02:22.539 --> 00:02:24.789
I wasn't sure if it was still
the middle of the night,

00:02:24.789 --> 00:02:27.059
so I didn't open my eyes right away.

00:02:27.059 --> 00:02:30.095
One thing I was sure about though,

00:02:30.095 --> 00:02:33.857
there was something lodged under my back

00:02:33.857 --> 00:02:36.754
that hadn't been there when I fell asleep.

00:02:36.754 --> 00:02:40.956
I shifted my body very
slightly from side to side.

00:02:40.956 --> 00:02:44.981
Whatever was under
there was hard yet soft.

00:02:44.981 --> 00:02:48.148
It was about the size of a small body.

00:02:49.118 --> 00:02:51.037
A fairy's body.

00:02:51.037 --> 00:02:52.694
Oh shit.

00:02:52.694 --> 00:02:56.861
I was laying on top of the
tooth fairy's dead body.

00:02:57.878 --> 00:03:00.616
I literally froze in fear.

00:03:00.616 --> 00:03:03.356
Before you ask, I don't sleep
with any stuffed animals

00:03:03.356 --> 00:03:05.362
on my bed, this is
literally the only thing

00:03:05.362 --> 00:03:06.770
it could have been.

00:03:06.770 --> 00:03:09.150
I realized I must have rolled
on top of her while she

00:03:09.150 --> 00:03:10.478
was trying to take my tooth.

00:03:10.478 --> 00:03:13.045
Oh my god, did she suffocate?

00:03:13.045 --> 00:03:15.219
Did I break all her bones?

00:03:15.219 --> 00:03:18.674
I had no way of knowing,
but one thing I did know,

00:03:18.674 --> 00:03:20.793
I had just killed someone.

00:03:20.793 --> 00:03:22.970
I just killed the woman
responsible for exchanging

00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:25.601
all the world's teeth for money.

00:03:25.601 --> 00:03:28.199
As far as I knew, I was the
most recent kid on earth

00:03:28.199 --> 00:03:29.656
to have lost a tooth.

00:03:29.656 --> 00:03:31.217
Everyone in my class knew.

00:03:31.217 --> 00:03:33.174
My parents knew, my siblings knew.

00:03:33.174 --> 00:03:34.576
There was a tooth trail.

00:03:34.576 --> 00:03:37.008
When the authorities catch
wind of her disappearance,

00:03:37.008 --> 00:03:39.051
they're coming for me first.

00:03:39.051 --> 00:03:40.693
I had to get rid of the evidence.

00:03:40.693 --> 00:03:43.491
I decided that first and
foremost, I was gonna need

00:03:43.491 --> 00:03:46.559
to make it look like the
tooth fairy had shown up.

00:03:46.559 --> 00:03:49.134
I decided I was going to take my tooth out

00:03:49.134 --> 00:03:52.713
from under my pillow and throw
it down the garbage disposal.

00:03:52.713 --> 00:03:55.147
I wasn't allowed to use
the garbage disposal,

00:03:55.147 --> 00:03:58.151
but I figured the next
time my mom turned it on,

00:03:58.151 --> 00:04:00.532
the evidence would be destroyed forever.

00:04:00.532 --> 00:04:04.068
Next, I was gonna steal a
dollar out of my dad's wallet.

00:04:04.068 --> 00:04:07.267
I was gonna take the dollar
and place it under my pillow

00:04:07.267 --> 00:04:09.745
so that way when the police showed up,

00:04:09.745 --> 00:04:12.880
I could show them the dollar,
they'd know the tooth fairy

00:04:12.880 --> 00:04:15.660
had shown up to my house
and they'd move on.

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:19.280
That left one more problem
for me to deal with.

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:23.340
How was I going to
dispose of this dead body

00:04:23.340 --> 00:04:25.935
without my mom finding out?

00:04:25.935 --> 00:04:30.626
Looking back only now do I
realize how truly fucked up

00:04:30.626 --> 00:04:32.619
this next train of thought was.

00:04:32.619 --> 00:04:36.543
My first thought was to
throw her body in my bathroom

00:04:36.543 --> 00:04:38.921
trash can and cover her with toilet paper.

00:04:38.921 --> 00:04:40.590
The more I thought about it,

00:04:40.590 --> 00:04:42.479
I figured it was just too risky.

00:04:42.479 --> 00:04:44.492
My mom would definitely see the body,

00:04:44.492 --> 00:04:46.162
so I scratched it.

00:04:46.162 --> 00:04:48.622
I definitely couldn't throw
her body in the huge trash cans

00:04:48.622 --> 00:04:49.912
in our side yard.

00:04:49.912 --> 00:04:52.743
For all I knew, our garbage
men were huge snitches.

00:04:52.743 --> 00:04:55.018
This idea, out of the question.

00:04:55.018 --> 00:04:59.000
She was probably too big
to flush down the toilet.

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:01.909
Do I dump her body in
the kitchen trash can?

00:05:01.909 --> 00:05:04.785
My dad was always snooping around there.

00:05:04.785 --> 00:05:06.825
I couldn't risk her
dropping the tooth fairy's

00:05:06.825 --> 00:05:10.558
mangled, bloody body at
my dad's feet like she did

00:05:10.558 --> 00:05:13.164
with the rats and birds
she found in our backyard.

00:05:13.164 --> 00:05:14.511
Backyard.

00:05:14.511 --> 00:05:16.270
The backyard.

00:05:16.270 --> 00:05:17.228
That was it!

00:05:17.228 --> 00:05:19.704
I would bury her in a
shoe box in my backyard

00:05:19.704 --> 00:05:22.760
just like I did with
my dead hamster Carmel.

00:05:22.760 --> 00:05:24.716
May she rest in peace.

00:05:24.716 --> 00:05:27.091
I decided I'd bury her
in the exact same spot

00:05:27.091 --> 00:05:29.524
as my hamster so that way, if the police,

00:05:29.524 --> 00:05:34.028
I don't know, brought some
sort of cadaver sniffing dog

00:05:34.028 --> 00:05:36.413
to the house, I could
assure them that the only

00:05:36.413 --> 00:05:39.380
dead body on this property
was that of a hamster.

00:05:39.380 --> 00:05:40.384
Alibis, baby.

00:05:40.384 --> 00:05:41.402
Okay.

00:05:41.402 --> 00:05:43.397
I think we've got a plan here.

00:05:43.397 --> 00:05:46.826
I'd store her in a shoe box
in my closet until sundown.

00:05:46.826 --> 00:05:49.578
In the dead of night, I'd
take my plastic shovel

00:05:49.578 --> 00:05:52.137
that I used to build sand
castles at the beach with

00:05:52.137 --> 00:05:55.576
and I'd dig a shallow grave
by the fence in my backyard.

00:05:55.576 --> 00:05:59.233
It was the perfect cover-up
to an accidental crime.

00:05:59.233 --> 00:06:01.032
Throughout this entire planning process,

00:06:01.032 --> 00:06:02.989
I still hadn't opened my eyes.

00:06:02.989 --> 00:06:05.208
I seriously hadn't moved a single inch

00:06:05.208 --> 00:06:06.750
in what felt like an hour.

00:06:06.750 --> 00:06:09.362
I knew that eventually
I had to open my eyes,

00:06:09.362 --> 00:06:12.627
sit up, and put my plan into motion.

00:06:12.627 --> 00:06:15.797
I had to face the facts,
look straight into her cold,

00:06:15.797 --> 00:06:20.706
dead fairy eyes and finally
accept what I had done.

00:06:20.706 --> 00:06:23.024
The clock says it's 7 a.m.
so it's definitely morning

00:06:23.024 --> 00:06:24.184
at this point.

00:06:24.184 --> 00:06:27.627
I slowly sat up, my heart
beating out of my chest,

00:06:27.627 --> 00:06:31.667
and that's when I realized
the thing I had been laying on

00:06:31.667 --> 00:06:34.334
this entire time was my own arm.

00:06:36.217 --> 00:06:39.728
That's right, at some point
during my stress-fueled slumber,

00:06:39.728 --> 00:06:43.828
my arm had lodged itself
under my back and was now

00:06:43.828 --> 00:06:45.257
completely numb.

00:06:45.257 --> 00:06:48.366
From the tips of my finger
to the top of my shoulder,

00:06:48.366 --> 00:06:49.957
couldn't feel a thing.

00:06:49.957 --> 00:06:54.280
I had been laying on my
own arm for the past hour

00:06:54.280 --> 00:06:56.638
while I devised a plan
to cover up the murder

00:06:56.638 --> 00:06:57.820
of the tooth fairy.

00:06:57.820 --> 00:07:01.682
I have never been so relieved
in my life to know that,

00:07:01.682 --> 00:07:04.747
one, I wasn't a cold-blooded murderer.

00:07:04.747 --> 00:07:07.075
Two, I wouldn't have
to talk to the police,

00:07:07.075 --> 00:07:09.173
or any strange adult for that matter.

00:07:09.173 --> 00:07:13.060
And most importantly, three,
my mom wouldn't be mad at me.

00:07:13.060 --> 00:07:15.501
When you're seven years old,
there is nothing scarier

00:07:15.501 --> 00:07:17.168
than disappointing your parents.

00:07:17.168 --> 00:07:20.189
Looking back, the worst part
of this story is that when

00:07:20.189 --> 00:07:22.990
I did go to look under my pillow
to see what the tooth fairy

00:07:22.990 --> 00:07:25.980
had left me, my tooth
was still sitting there,

00:07:25.980 --> 00:07:29.684
right where I had left it
in a plastic zip lock bag.

00:07:29.684 --> 00:07:33.601
My parents forgot that
I had even lost a tooth,

00:07:33.601 --> 00:07:35.715
and they never came to
swap it out for money

00:07:35.715 --> 00:07:37.600
like they were supposed to.

00:07:37.600 --> 00:07:41.322
So not only was I now
moneyless and exhausted,

00:07:41.322 --> 00:07:44.062
but I was gonna have to go
through a whole nother night

00:07:44.062 --> 00:07:46.335
of waiting for the tooth fairy to show up.

00:07:46.335 --> 00:07:48.256
Thanks mom and dad.

00:07:48.256 --> 00:07:50.756
(jazzy music)

